.nh
.TH "PB-RECIPE-CREATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recipe-create - Create a recipe from a file and print its token once


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recipe create -f <file> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a recipe from a .jsonc file (JSON with comments); its name is the file's base name (ci.jsonc
makes ci). The file is checked on this computer first, with file:line:col errors.
The token is made here and printed once: save it as the secret PB_RECIPE. Paperboat
stores only a hash of it and can never read the ENV vaults the recipe reads.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--file\fP=""
	the recipe file (.jsonc)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON (the token included, once)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recipe create -f ci.jsonc
  pb recipe create -f ci.jsonc --workspace acme
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recipe(1)\fP
